S. (Physics/Mathematics, Russia), an M. Phil (International ... \",\"title\":\"https://crown.ucsc.edu/sfc/past-keynote-speakers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... Neurosurgeon George Mandybur, MD, first implanted the Omnia system at the Mayfield Spine Surgery Center in September 2019. Marc Orlando, MD, a specialist in physical medicine and rehabilitation, performed the stimulator trial six weeks earlier.\\n\\nApril 2019 – Mayfield expands its role in national clinical data registries that seek ... \",\"title\":\"https://mayfieldclinic.com/history.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Similar results have been noted in analyses of national behavior analysis conferences (e.g., ABAI; Nosik et al., 2019). Thus, there is an opportunity to improve the parity of keynote and invited speakers at conferences. The first step in doing so is to collect baseline data and provide ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10169981/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d7\",\"snippet\":\" ... Calls for papers – Conferences taking place in September 2019\\ndate: 2018-01-26\\n---\\nSecrets: 22nd International Colloquium of American Studies\\n\\nFaculty of Arts, Palacký University in Olomouc, Czech Republic, 12-14 September 2019\\n\\nExtended deadline for proposals: 20 June 2019\\n\\nPlenary speakers:\\n\\nPhilip McGowan (Queen's University Belfast ... \",\"title\":\"https://essenglish.org/cfp/conf1909/\"}],\"query\":\"Philip Tew keynote speaker 2019 conference\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... ROD MENGHAM\\n\\nRod Mengham is author of several poetry publications, including Grimspound & Inhabiting Art (Carcanet, 2018), the vase in pieces (Oystercatcher, 2019) and of translations, including Speedometry [poems by Andrzej Sosnowski] (Contraband, 2014) and Flatsharing [poems by Anne Portugal] (Equipage, forthcoming). He has been the co-editor and ... \",\"title\":\"https://societyofauthors.org/2020/06/18/winners-of-the-2020-society-of-authors-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2009)\\n\\nWork from a wide range of young London-based poets\\n\\n- edited Jeff Hilson, The Reality Street Book of Sonnets (Reality Street, 2008)\\n\\nA superb gathering of what a huge number of contemporary British poets (largely) are doing with and to this inescapable and foundational form.\\n\\n- edited Rod ... \",\"title\":\"http://www.modernpoetry.org.uk/anth.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... One main aim of this seminar is to assist graduate students in the period in laying the basis of a research community amongst themselves. The hope is that it will continue to evolve (as it has in past years) into a student-led reading group, meeting informally and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.english.cam.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/Post-1830_Info.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... Joel Leonard Katz, Rod Mengham, Malcolm Sinclair, Adam Zdrodowski, Equipage, 2007), A Marzipan Factory (trans. Adam Zdrodowski, Otoliths, 2010), Kopenhaga (trans. Piotr Gwiazda, Zephyr Press, 2013), Let's Go Back to the Mainland (trans. Agnieszka Pokojska, Červená Barva Press, 2014), Zero Visibility (trans. Piotr Gwiazda, Phoneme Media, 2017 ... \",\"title\":\"http://www.thelostbookshelf.com/w.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... senses for a lifetime\\\" (22M€ Grant)\\n\\n-\\n\\n2009-2020 Director of the Research Centre: Vision Institute, UMR S 968 Inserm, UM80 Sorbonne Univ./ UMR 7210 CNRS\\n\\n-\\n\\n2005-2021 Director of the Clinical Investigation Centre –503 INSERM/ Quinze-Vingts National, Paris\\n\\n-\\n\\n2007-2017 Coordinator of the Foundation Fighting Blindness Paris ... \",\"title\":\"https://ophthalmology.pitt.edu/people/jose-alain-sahel-md\"}],\"query\":\"Rod Mengham research group coordinator 2009 founded\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_94f31c59c5ef4d4e96d69e86"},{"content":"Let me find the Rod Mengham section in d15 to get more details about him.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d15\", \"text\": \"ROD MENGHAM\"}","name":"find"},"id":"call_ee8914608ecc45088b2c5d11","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"case_sensitive\":true,\"document\":\"d15\",\"executed\":true,\"kind\":\"positions_not_evidence\",\"matches\":[{\"end\":27090,\"excerpt\":\"S PREVIOUSLY LIVED IN HAYES, RUISLIP, COLORADO, AND INDIA.\\n\\nROD MENGHAM\\n\\nRod Mengham is author of several poetry publications, incl\",\"start\":27079}],\"next_start\":null,\"ok\":true,\"snapshot\":\"0f5a823afe70f8c6fe64739371a3059701ee5b8b10366534f881544a2343eafb\"}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_ee8914608ecc45088b2c5d11"},{"content":"","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d15\", \"start\": 27079, \"length\": 2000}","name":"read"},"id":"call_df60d2f4dc5b4af78bc284b4","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d15\",\"document_chars\":29760,\"end\":29079,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e6\",\"sha256\":\"1d5f847f53f60f93efcfe6e593c3e8b66472f112f8a74e6057ed3d4b6b6e6bb5\",\"snapshot\":\"0f5a823afe70f8c6fe64739371a3059701ee5b8b10366534f881544a2343eafb\",\"start\":27079,\"text\":\"ROD MENGHAM\\n\\nRod Mengham is author of several poetry publications, including Grimspound & Inhabiting Art (Carcanet, 2018), the vase in pieces (Oystercatcher, 2019) and of translations, including Speedometry [poems by Andrzej Sosnowski] (Contraband, 2014) and Flatsharing [poems by Anne Portugal] (Equipage, forthcoming). He has been the co-editor and co-translator of multiple anthologies, co-wrote Thomas Hardy's Shorter Fiction (EUP, 2007), published monographs on Dickens, Emily Bronte and Henry Green; and The Descent of Language (1993) and edited several essay collections. Between 1992 and 2002, he was co-organiser of the annual Cambridge Conference of Contemporary Poetry and since 1992 has been the publisher of Equipage. Rod is Reader in Modern English Literature at Cambridge University, and a Fellow of Jesus College. He has also curated many exhibitions of contemporary art since 2003, and has made several films with the artist Marc Atkins (soundingpolefilms) as well as the text + image publication Still Moving (London: Veer Publications, 2014). ROD IS ORIGINALLY FROM WEST SUSSEX AND NOW LIVES IN CAMBRIDGE.\\n\\nTHE TRAVELLING SCHOLARSHIPS\\n\\nThe Travelling Scholarships are awarded to British writers to enable engagement with writers abroad. Judged by Tahmima Anam, Aida Edemariam, Adam O'Riordan, Sameer Rahim and Gary Younge. Previous recipients have included Dylan Thomas, Laurie Lee, Margaret Drabble and Helen Simpson. Total prize fund: £8,000.\\n\\nAWARDED TO FIVE BRITISH WRITERS TO ENABLE TRAVEL AND ENGAGEMENT WITH WRITERS ABROAD. £1,600 EACH TO:\\n\\n- LUKE BROWN, books editor, columnist, lecturer, and author of My Biggest Lie\\n\\n- INUA ELLAMS, a poet, playwright, and designer who founded The Midnight Run\\n\\n- GEORGINA LAWTON, journalist, travel writer, and author of Raceless\\n\\n- NEIL ROLLINSON, previous Cholmondeley Award recipient whose most recent book Talking Dead was shortlisted for the Costa Poetry Prize\\n\\n- AHDAF SOUEIF, author of Book Prize shortlisted novel The Map of Love\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":29079,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_df60d2f4dc5b4af78bc284b4"},{"content":"I have strong evidence that Rod Mengham is the convenor of the Cambridge Centenary Symposium and wrote about Henry Green. Now I need to verify the other clues: the 2018 Routledge book co-edited with Philip Tew, the research group founded in 2009, the 2012 article, and Philip Tew as a 2019 keynote speaker. Let me search for these.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Philip Tew Rod Mengham Routledge 2018 book\", \"Philip Tew keynote speaker 2019 conference\", \"Rod Mengham 2012 article published\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_760fa083bdf34914bbf0f95d","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Rod Mengham coordinator research group 2009\", \"Rod Mengham Philip Tew co-edited Routledge\", \"Philip Tew 2019 keynote plenary speaker\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_1da4895a9f014792ada3f3e0","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... Stories of Survival (2001); with Philip Tew he has co-edited Contemporary British Fiction (2003) and British Fiction Today (2006). He has edited fiction by Dickens and E.M.Forster, and is a poet whose most recent book is Unsung: New and Selected Poems (1996; second ed. 2001 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.english.cam.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/Post-1830_Info.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... based poets\\n\\n- edited Jeff Hilson, The Reality Street Book of Sonnets (Reality Street, 2008)\\n\\nA superb gathering of what a huge number of contemporary British poets (largely) are doing with and to this inescapable and foundational form.\\n\\n- edited Rod Mengham & John Kinsella, Vanishing Points: New Modernist Poems (Salt ... \",\"title\":\"http://www.modernpoetry.org.uk/anth.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\"